Z||000002||rodmcneill||12-20-2001||10:53 AM||||I just replaced mine recently with both inner and outer tie rod ends. My bushing was steel instead of plastic. You do have to take the rack completely apart to replace the bushing.Make sure you spray the 4 rack bolts with lots of liquid wrench before attempting to remove them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-20-2001||12:54 PM||||I've only done an 88 rack bushing but I didn't have to take the rack apart. Pop the tie rod end loose from the steering knuckle and unscrew the inner tie rod end( can be tricky), dog out the plastic bushing and slide the new one on. Put in the rivets and you're done. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zoom88||12-20-2001||02:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>I've only done an 88 rack bushing but I didn't have to take the rack apart. Pop the tie rod end loose from the steering knuckle and unscrew the inner tie rod end( can be tricky), dog out the plastic bushing and slide the new one on. Put in the rivets and you're done. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Any tips on that tricky part, I am getting ready to do my 88 passenger side inner tie-rod. Got the bushing from Rodney. How hard and what did you have to do to get the rivets in?<P>||||reg||1
